I like the sound of Duane's approach, up to the last line. Maybe I'm misunderstanding, but it would be a mistake to treat only positive locations as 'detectors'. Also: from the description it seems people were let loose to go where they liked; this is OK if coverage was effectively complete and more or less uniform, otherwise I think we should be moving to formal (probability-based) spatial sampling designs.

The problem for Melissa will be in how to implement the advice...

