Sure - I'm not questioning your design.Just felt the need to assert the broader principle.When that becomes important depends on scale: in a large region with relatively small detection distances one shouldn't just go where the animals are (i.e. preferentially sample areas of high density)(which is not what you're doing). There's not such an issue with how detection effort is configured within home ranges unless it leads to biased estimates of sigma because of range alignment.

Murray

